{[#]} 1. Bd4# {Morphy’s Mate is named after the legendary American chess
player, Paul Morphy. The checkmate is executed by a bishop and rook: Morphy's
mate is a common method of checkmating. It was named after Paul Morphy . It
works by using the bishop to attack the black king and a rook and Black's own
pawn to confine it. In many respects it is very similar to the Corner mate.} *

